  <diagram id="3VZAMd3l9Ok4oFObbLUY" name="3-Questions-Assumptions">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1830" dy="2505" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <UserObject label="" mermaidData="{&#xa;  &quot;data&quot;: &quot;flowchart TB\n    %% ================= Title =================\n    Title[\&quot;&lt;b&gt;Part C — Questions, Assumptions &amp; Contradictions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Name: [Your Name] | ID: [Your ID] | Group: [Your Group]\&quot;]\n    style Title fill:#1e293b,stroke:#0f172a,color:#ffffff,stroke-width:3px,font-size:18px\n\n    %% ================= 1. Questions =================\n    subgraph QUESTIONS [1. Questions]\n        direction TB\n        Q_TABLE[\n        \&quot;&lt;b&gt;#&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;SRS Section&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Question&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;Q1&lt;/b&gt; | 7.1 Branches and Staff | What is the fallback if both the branch manager resigns and the regional director is temporarily unavailable to take over? Does the system need to log acting managers?&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;Q2&lt;/b&gt; | 7.16 Payments | For corporate clients who receive a single monthly invoice instead of paying per rental, does the system track credit billing cycles and corporate invoice IDs, or is corporate invoicing completely handled offline in Phase 1?&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;Q3&lt;/b&gt; | 7.15 Maintenance | If a vehicle is currently rented out or reserved, does opening a job card automatically flag a conflict or cancel upcoming reservations for that vehicle?&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;Q4&lt;/b&gt; | 7.8 Corporate Contracts | Can a corporate client have multiple active contracts simultaneously with overlapping validity periods but different discount rates, or only one active contract at a time?\&quot;\n        ]\n    end\n    style Q_TABLE fill:#f8fafc,stroke:#cbd5e1,color:#0f172a,stroke-width:1.5px,text-align:left\n\n    %% ================= 2. Assumptions =================\n    subgraph ASSUMPTIONS [2. Assumptions]\n        direction TB\n        A_TABLE[\n        \&quot;&lt;b&gt;#&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;SRS Section&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Assumption Made in Design&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;A1&lt;/b&gt; | 7.3 Fleet &amp; Pricing | To handle luxury cars with custom prices (e.g., Mercedes S-Class mentioned by the COO), we assumed an optional CustomDailyPrice attribute on the VEHICLE table that overrides the standard VEHICLE_CATEGORY daily rate when not NULL.&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;A2&lt;/b&gt; | 7.10 Loyalty Program | Assumed loyalty tiers (Silver, Gold, Platinum) are derived dynamically from the cumulative points balance or updated via business logic, and that points cannot fall below zero.&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;A3&lt;/b&gt; | 7.12 Rentals | Assumed an extension creates a new RENTAL record that references the previous rental via a 1:1 recursive foreign key (ParentRentalNo), establishing an audit chain of extensions.&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;A4&lt;/b&gt; | 7.14 Damage Reports | Assumed damage reports are uniquely identified in combination with the rental number (RentalNo, ReportNo), forming a weak entity pattern with external photo links stored in a separate multivalued table (DAMAGE_PHOTO).&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;A5&lt;/b&gt; | 7.7 Customers | Assumed CustomerType (&#39;Individual&#39; vs &#39;Corporate&#39;) is a disjoint specialization; an individual customer record is kept completely separate from an authorized corporate driver record, even if the same physical person holds both roles.\&quot;\n        ]\n    end\n    style A_TABLE fill:#f8fafc,stroke:#cbd5e1,color:#0f172a,stroke-width:1.5px,text-align:left\n\n    %% ================= 3. Contradictions =================\n    subgraph CONTRADICTIONS [3. Contradictions]\n        direction TB\n        C_TABLE[\n        \&quot;&lt;b&gt;#&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Sections Involved&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Contradiction Details&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;C1&lt;/b&gt; | Section 7.3 vs Section 8 (Fleet Manager Statement) | In Section 7.3, the text states that every vehicle is registered under one home branch but &#39;may be physically at another branch at any moment&#39;. However, in Section 8, the Fleet Manager insists that &#39;no car should ever be transferred to the same branch it&#39;s already in.&#39; If vehicles can end up at another branch via one-way rentals (Section 7.11 / 7.12) without a formal transfer record, the current branch location could drift unless every return updates the vehicle&#39;s CurrentBranchCode.&lt;br&gt;\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;C2&lt;/b&gt; | Section 7.7 vs Section 8 (Corporate Accounts Statement) | Section 7.7 states: &#39;Corporate clients give DriveNow a list of authorized drivers... These drivers are only known through their company... If a corporate account is closed, its driver list has no meaning anymore.&#39; But in Section 8, Ms. Rana Adel states: &#39;Some corporate drivers are also individual customers with us. For example, an engineer rents for work through his company, and in the summer rents for his family on his own account.&#39; The contradiction is that their corporate driver profile cannot be merged directly with their individual customer profile because corporate drivers are weak entities owned by the corporation without independent customer IDs.\&quot;\n        ]\n    end\n    style C_TABLE fill:#f8fafc,stroke:#cbd5e1,color:#0f172a,stroke-width:1.5px,text-align:left&quot;,&#xa;  &quot;config&quot;: null,&#xa;  &quot;version&quot;: &quot;12&quot;&#xa;}" id="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-1">
          <mxCell connectable="0" parent="1" style="group;transparentBounds=1;editIcon=1;lockedGroup=0;groupPadding=10;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="3. Contradictions" mermaidId="n:CONTRADICTIONS" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#FFF7ED;strokeColor=#FB923C;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Recursive;fontSize=14;shadow=1;shadowColor=#000000;shadowOffsetX=4;shadowOffsetY=4;shadowBlur=0;shadowOpacity=6;" mermaidBaseValue="3. Contradictions" id="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-2">
          <mxCell parent="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#FFF7ED;strokeColor=#FB923C;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Recursive;fontSize=14;shadow=1;shadowColor=#000000;shadowOffsetX=4;shadowOffsetY=4;shadowBlur=0;shadowOpacity=6;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DRecursive;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="2469" width="200" x="410" y="58" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;#&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Sections Involved&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Contradiction Details&lt;/b&gt;&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;C1&lt;/b&gt; | Section 7.3 vs Section 8 (Fleet Manager Statement) | In Section 7.3, the text states that every vehicle is registered under one home branch but &#39;may be physically at another branch at any moment&#39;. However, in Section 8, the Fleet Manager insists that &#39;no car should ever be transferred to the same branch it&#39;s already in.&#39; If vehicles can end up at another branch via one-way rentals (Section 7.11 / 7.12) without a formal transfer record, the current branch location could drift unless every return updates the vehicle&#39;s CurrentBranchCode.&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;C2&lt;/b&gt; | Section 7.7 vs Section 8 (Corporate Accounts Statement) | Section 7.7 states: &#39;Corporate clients give DriveNow a list of authorized drivers... These drivers are only known through their company... If a corporate account is closed, its driver list has no meaning anymore.&#39; But in Section 8, Ms. Rana Adel states: &#39;Some corporate drivers are also individual customers with us. For example, an engineer rents for work through his company, and in the summer rents for his family on his own account.&#39; The contradiction is that their corporate driver profile cannot be merged directly with their individual customer profile because corporate drivers are weak entities owned by the corporation without independent customer IDs." mermaidId="n:C_TABLE" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.5;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#0f172a;fontFamily=Recursive;fontSize=14;shadow=1;shadowColor=#000000;shadowOffsetX=4;shadowOffsetY=4;shadowBlur=0;shadowOpacity=6;" mermaidBaseValue="&lt;b&gt;#&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Sections Involved&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Contradiction Details&lt;/b&gt;&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;C1&lt;/b&gt; | Section 7.3 vs Section 8 (Fleet Manager Statement) | In Section 7.3, the text states that every vehicle is registered under one home branch but &#39;may be physically at another branch at any moment&#39;. However, in Section 8, the Fleet Manager insists that &#39;no car should ever be transferred to the same branch it&#39;s already in.&#39; If vehicles can end up at another branch via one-way rentals (Section 7.11 / 7.12) without a formal transfer record, the current branch location could drift unless every return updates the vehicle&#39;s CurrentBranchCode.&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;C2&lt;/b&gt; | Section 7.7 vs Section 8 (Corporate Accounts Statement) | Section 7.7 states: &#39;Corporate clients give DriveNow a list of authorized drivers... These drivers are only known through their company... If a corporate account is closed, its driver list has no meaning anymore.&#39; But in Section 8, Ms. Rana Adel states: &#39;Some corporate drivers are also individual customers with us. For example, an engineer rents for work through his company, and in the summer rents for his family on his own account.&#39; The contradiction is that their corporate driver profile cannot be merged directly with their individual customer profile because corporate drivers are weak entities owned by the corporation without independent customer IDs." id="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-3">
          <mxCell parent="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-2" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.5;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#0f172a;fontFamily=Recursive;fontSize=14;shadow=1;shadowColor=#000000;shadowOffsetX=4;shadowOffsetY=4;shadowBlur=0;shadowOpacity=6;labelWidth=120;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DRecursive;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="2397" width="152" x="24" y="48" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="2. Assumptions" mermaidId="n:ASSUMPTIONS" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#F0FDFA;strokeColor=#2DD4BF;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Recursive;fontSize=14;shadow=1;shadowColor=#000000;shadowOffsetX=4;shadowOffsetY=4;shadowBlur=0;shadowOpacity=6;" mermaidBaseValue="2. Assumptions" id="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-4">
          <mxCell parent="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#F0FDFA;strokeColor=#2DD4BF;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Recursive;fontSize=14;shadow=1;shadowColor=#000000;shadowOffsetX=4;shadowOffsetY=4;shadowBlur=0;shadowOpacity=6;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DRecursive;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="2784" width="200" x="650" y="-100" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;#&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;SRS Section&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Assumption Made in Design&lt;/b&gt;&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A1&lt;/b&gt; | 7.3 Fleet &amp; Pricing | To handle luxury cars with custom prices (e.g., Mercedes S-Class mentioned by the COO), we assumed an optional CustomDailyPrice attribute on the VEHICLE table that overrides the standard VEHICLE_CATEGORY daily rate when not NULL.&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A2&lt;/b&gt; | 7.10 Loyalty Program | Assumed loyalty tiers (Silver, Gold, Platinum) are derived dynamically from the cumulative points balance or updated via business logic, and that points cannot fall below zero.&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A3&lt;/b&gt; | 7.12 Rentals | Assumed an extension creates a new RENTAL record that references the previous rental via a 1:1 recursive foreign key (ParentRentalNo), establishing an audit chain of extensions.&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A4&lt;/b&gt; | 7.14 Damage Reports | Assumed damage reports are uniquely identified in combination with the rental number (RentalNo, ReportNo), forming a weak entity pattern with external photo links stored in a separate multivalued table (DAMAGE_PHOTO).&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A5&lt;/b&gt; | 7.7 Customers | Assumed CustomerType (&#39;Individual&#39; vs &#39;Corporate&#39;) is a disjoint specialization; an individual customer record is kept completely separate from an authorized corporate driver record, even if the same physical person holds both roles." mermaidId="n:A_TABLE" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.5;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#0f172a;fontFamily=Recursive;fontSize=14;shadow=1;shadowColor=#000000;shadowOffsetX=4;shadowOffsetY=4;shadowBlur=0;shadowOpacity=6;" mermaidBaseValue="&lt;b&gt;#&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;SRS Section&lt;/b&gt; | &lt;b&gt;Assumption Made in Design&lt;/b&gt;&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A1&lt;/b&gt; | 7.3 Fleet &amp; Pricing | To handle luxury cars with custom prices (e.g., Mercedes S-Class mentioned by the COO), we assumed an optional CustomDailyPrice attribute on the VEHICLE table that overrides the standard VEHICLE_CATEGORY daily rate when not NULL.&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A2&lt;/b&gt; | 7.10 Loyalty Program | Assumed loyalty tiers (Silver, Gold, Platinum) are derived dynamically from the cumulative points balance or updated via business logic, and that points cannot fall below zero.&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A3&lt;/b&gt; | 7.12 Rentals | Assumed an extension creates a new RENTAL record that references the previous rental via a 1:1 recursive foreign key (ParentRentalNo), establishing an audit chain of extensions.&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A4&lt;/b&gt; | 7.14 Damage Reports | Assumed damage reports are uniquely identified in combination with the rental number (RentalNo, ReportNo), forming a weak entity pattern with external photo links stored in a separate multivalued table (DAMAGE_PHOTO).&#xa;&#xa;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;A5&lt;/b&gt; | 7.7 Customers | Assumed CustomerType (&#39;Individual&#39; vs &#39;Corporate&#39;) is a disjoint specialization; an individual customer record is kept completely separate from an authorized corporate driver record, even if the same physical person holds both roles." id="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-5">
          <mxCell parent="6yz99jHD4Rz_dEeoc8f4-4" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.5;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#0f172a;fontFamily=Recursive;fontSize=14;shadow=1;shadowColor=#000000;shadowOffsetX=4;shadowOffsetY=4;shadowBlur=0;shadowOpacity=6;labelWidth=120;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DRecursive;" vertex="1">
